    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0020" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/864</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Delegate</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 420</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1937-05-07"
                            >May 7, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received May 18.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit in Spanish
                    text and English translation a memorandum of the conversation which took place
                    at the dinner with General Justo, President of the Argentine Republic, on April
                    29. The dinner was reported briefly in my telegram No. 63 of April 30, 6
                        p.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d8-f1"/></p>
                <p>Each of the three delegates participating in the dinner have retained one signed
                    copy. This memorandum is being made available only to the Brazilian and Chilean
                    Foreign Offices and the State Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spruille Braden</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d8-a1.xml" xpointer="d8-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
